{"chunk_id": "027394239411", "text": "While encamped on Mount Kailasha during his campaign against the gods, Ravana wanders beneath the moonlit forests, where music of Apsaras and celestial beings fills the night and stirs his desire. He encounters the beautiful nymph Rambha on her way to meet Nalakuvara, the virtuous son of Kubera. Despite her pleas that she is effectively his daughter\u2011in\u2011law and under his protection, Ravana dismisses her arguments and violently ravishes her. Shaken and dishonored, Rambha goes to Nalakuvara and recounts the assault. Furious, Nalakuvara performs a ritual and curses Ravana: if he ever forces himself upon a woman who does not desire him, his head will shatter into seven pieces. The gods rejoice, recognizing that this curse will shape Ravana\u2019s fate and limit his future crimes.\nRavana assaults the apsara Rambha despite her pleas, prompting Nalakuvara to curse him that forced violation will shatter his head.\nThemes: sexual violence, curse and consequence, abuse of power, divine justice, foreshadowing Ravana's limits", "vector": [-0.006432811263948679, -0.019475234672427177, 0.007629613392055035, 0.008595215156674385, 0.0006749011809006333, 0.007575213443487883, -0.010805219411849976, -0.013967224396765232, -0.01774803176522255, -0.027852850034832954, 0.007724813651293516, 0.01137642003595829, 0.026424847543239594, -0.0026231047231703997, -0.008921615779399872, 0.007500413339585066, 0.04558728262782097, -0.01957043446600437, 0.025391245260834694, -0.01729923114180565, 0.0018003032309934497, 0.002196403918787837, -0.021556038409471512, -0.00034765060991048813, -0.036856066435575485, 0.01115201972424984, 0.0217464379966259, -0.035958465188741684, 0.01362722460180521, 0.0026520045939832926, -0.004821208771318197, -0.007133212871849537, 0.00965601671487093, -0.008452415466308594, -0.027268048375844955, -0.007935614325106144, -0.008132814429700375, -0.017952032387256622, 0.003411906072869897, 0.009717217646539211, 0.0004322257